cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite it as below. The associated paper is
  in preparation; this file will be updated with the article reference once published.
title: "From Geographic Coverage to Operational Resilience: official implementation"
abstract: >-
  Official implementation of a data-driven framework for medical-drone hub planning
  during Hajj, comparing geographic coverage benchmarks against an operational-resilient
  mixed-integer linear program with fleet capacity, endurance, response-time and backup
  accessibility requirements.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Al-Hindawi
    given-names: Firas
    affiliation: "King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals"
  - family-names: Alhomaidhi
    given-names: Esam
    affiliation: "King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hindawi91/hajj-medical-drone-network"
keywords:
  - facility location
  - medical drones
  - Hajj
  - mass gatherings
  - mixed-integer programming
  - emergency logistics
  - OpenStreetMap
